---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc805.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope – the Definition of a Business" },
        { id: "s3", label: "The Acquisition Method – Overview" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Identifying the Acquirer and Acquisition Date" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Recognising and Measuring Identifiable Assets, Liabilities, and NCI" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Goodwill Measurement" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Noncontrolling Interest – Full Goodwill vs the IFRS 3 Choice" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Bargain Purchase Gains" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Acquisition-Related Costs" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Contingent Consideration" },
        { id: "s11", label: "The Measurement Period" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Worked Example – Full vs Partial Goodwill (NCI Choice)" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Worked Example – a Bargain Purchase Gain" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s16", label: "ASC 805 vs IFRS 3 – Comprehensive Comparison" },
        { id: "s17", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s18", label: "Related Topics" },
        { id: "s19", label: "Quick-Reference Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci"><div class="ctitle ci">Fair value at the moment control changes hands</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">When an entity obtains CONTROL of a business, that transaction is treated as a genuinely NEW measurement event – assets acquired and liabilities assumed are recognised at their ACQUISITION-DATE FAIR VALUES, capturing the full economics of the deal rather than carrying forward the target's old historical costs. ASC 805 governs this "acquisition method."</div></div>
      <div class="card cs"><div class="ctitle cs">A genuine joint-project standard, with one well-known remaining divergence</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 805 and IFRS 3 emerged from a JOINT FASB-IASB convergence project (completed around 2008-2009) and share the SAME fundamental acquisition-method structure. The single most significant remaining divergence is the NONCONTROLLING INTEREST measurement choice (Section 7) – worth knowing well, since it's the standout comparison point in an otherwise closely converged standard.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope – the Definition of a Business</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A simplified screen test, post-ASU 2017-01</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASU 2017-01 introduced a SCREEN test to simplify the often-contentious "is this a business or just an asset group" determination: if SUBSTANTIALLY ALL of the fair value of the gross assets acquired is CONCENTRATED in a single identifiable asset (or group of similar assets), the transaction is NOT a business – it is an ASSET ACQUISITION instead. Notably, IFRS 3 followed with its OWN broadly similar concentration test amendment in 2020 – a rare instance of IFRS adopting a structure closely modelled on a prior US GAAP change, making this a genuinely CONVERGED area today.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Acquisition Method – Overview</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Four core steps</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.3fr 2.7fr;"><span>Step</span><span>Description</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.3fr 2.7fr;"><span>1</span><span>Identify the acquirer</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.3fr 2.7fr;"><span>2</span><span>Determine the acquisition date</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.3fr 2.7fr;"><span>3</span><span>Recognise and measure identifiable assets acquired, liabilities assumed, and any noncontrolling interest at fair value</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.3fr 2.7fr;"><span>4</span><span>Recognise goodwill or a bargain purchase gain</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Identifying the Acquirer and Acquisition Date</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Substance over legal form</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The ACQUIRER is the entity that obtains CONTROL – not necessarily the legally acquiring entity (a "reverse acquisition" can occur when the legal acquirer is the accounting ACQUIREE). The ACQUISITION DATE is the date control is obtained, generally the closing date – the same identification principles IFRS 3 applies.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Recognising and Measuring Identifiable Assets, Liabilities, and NCI</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Fair value, with specific exceptions</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Identifiable assets acquired and liabilities assumed are recognised at ACQUISITION-DATE FAIR VALUE, with a handful of specific EXCEPTIONS to this general rule (e.g. income taxes measured per ASC 740 rather than fair value, certain employee benefit obligations measured per ASC 715, indemnification assets measured on the same basis as the indemnified item) – broadly the same general approach and exception list IFRS 3 applies.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Goodwill Measurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The same formula as IFRS 3</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:2.4fr 0.6fr;"><span>Component</span><span>Sign</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2.4fr 0.6fr;"><span>Consideration transferred (fair value)</span><span>+</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2.4fr 0.6fr;"><span>Fair value of any noncontrolling interest</span><span>+</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:2.4fr 0.6fr;"><span>Fair value of any previously held equity interest (step acquisitions)</span><span>+</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:2.4fr 0.6fr;"><span>Fair value of net identifiable assets acquired</span><span>−</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">The residual, if positive, is goodwill; if negative, it's a bargain purchase gain (Section 8).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Noncontrolling Interest – Full Goodwill vs the IFRS 3 Choice</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The standout remaining divergence</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">US GAAP REQUIRES noncontrolling interest (NCI) to be measured at FAIR VALUE – which effectively means the "FULL GOODWILL" method is the ONLY option: goodwill is measured as if the ENTIRE target (100%) were acquired at its implied fair value, with a proportionate share attributed to the NCI. IFRS 3 offers a GENUINE CHOICE, made on an ACQUISITION-BY-ACQUISITION basis: NCI may be measured EITHER at FAIR VALUE (the "full goodwill" method, matching the mandatory US approach), OR at the NCI's PROPORTIONATE SHARE of the acquiree's identifiable NET ASSETS (the "PARTIAL GOODWILL" method, which excludes the NCI's share of goodwill entirely). This is the single most significant divergence remaining in an otherwise closely converged standard – under IFRS, two seemingly similar acquisitions can produce DIFFERENT total reported goodwill purely based on which NCI measurement option is elected.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Bargain Purchase Gains</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Converged – immediate income recognition</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">If the net identifiable assets acquired EXCEED the consideration transferred (plus NCI and previously held interests) – a "bargain purchase" – the resulting GAIN is recognised IMMEDIATELY in EARNINGS at the acquisition date, after first reassessing whether all assets/liabilities were correctly identified and measured. The same immediate income statement recognition applies under IFRS 3.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Acquisition-Related Costs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Expensed, not capitalised – converged</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Costs the acquirer incurs in connection with the acquisition (legal, advisory, due diligence fees) are EXPENSED AS INCURRED, and are NOT included in the consideration transferred or capitalised as part of the acquired assets – the same treatment IFRS 3 requires.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Contingent Consideration</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair value at acquisition, then classification-dependent subsequent treatment</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Contingent consideration (e.g. an earnout) is measured at FAIR VALUE at the acquisition date and included in consideration transferred. Subsequently, LIABILITY-classified contingent consideration is REMEASURED each period with changes through EARNINGS; EQUITY-classified contingent consideration is NOT remeasured – the same classification-dependent approach IFRS 3 applies.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>The Measurement Period</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Up to one year to finalise provisional amounts</div><div style="font-size:var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">If initial accounting for a business combination is INCOMPLETE at the reporting date, the acquirer reports PROVISIONAL amounts, subsequently ADJUSTED retrospectively as new information about facts existing at the acquisition date comes to light – up to a MEASUREMENT PERIOD of ONE YEAR from the acquisition date – the same one-year measurement period IFRS 3 allows.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Worked Example – Full vs Partial Goodwill (NCI Choice)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The same acquisition, two different IFRS outcomes</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An 80% acquisition</div><div class="wk-body">An acquirer purchases 80% of a target for $8,000,000 cash. The target's identifiable net assets have a fair value of $9,000,000. The remaining 20% NCI has an implied fair value of $2,000,000 (based on the same per-share price paid for the 80% stake).</div><div class="wk-answer"><strong>Under US GAAP (mandatory full goodwill):</strong> Goodwill = ($8,000,000 + $2,000,000 NCI at fair value) minus $9,000,000 = <strong>$1,000,000</strong>.<br><strong>Under IFRS 3, full goodwill election:</strong> SAME calculation, SAME $1,000,000.<br><strong>Under IFRS 3, partial goodwill election:</strong> NCI measured at its proportionate share of net assets = 20% times $9,000,000 = $1,800,000 (not $2,000,000 fair value). Goodwill = ($8,000,000 + $1,800,000) minus $9,000,000 = <strong>$800,000</strong> – a LOWER total goodwill figure, and NCI itself is presented at a DIFFERENT amount, purely due to the election IFRS 3 permits but US GAAP does not.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Worked Example – a Bargain Purchase Gain</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognising a gain instead of goodwill</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An acquisition below net asset fair value</div><div class="wk-body">An acquirer purchases 100% of a distressed target for $5,000,000 cash. After reassessing all identifiable assets and liabilities, the target's net identifiable assets have a fair value of $6,200,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">Bargain purchase gain = $6,200,000 minus $5,000,000 = <strong>$1,200,000</strong>, recognised IMMEDIATELY in earnings at the acquisition date, after confirming the identification and measurement of all acquired items was performed correctly.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 805 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Name and description of the acquiree, acquisition date, and percentage of voting interests acquired</span><span>Fair value of consideration transferred, by major class</span><span>Amounts recognised for major classes of assets acquired and liabilities assumed</span><span>Amount of goodwill, and a qualitative description of factors comprising it</span><span>Amount and measurement basis of any noncontrolling interest</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an acquired set of activities/assets meets the definition of a "business"</span><span>Identifying the accounting acquirer, particularly in complex or reverse acquisition structures</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of identifiable intangible assets, contingent consideration, and NCI</span><span>Fair value of any previously held equity interest in a step acquisition</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>ASC 805 vs IFRS 3 – Comprehensive Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison – ASC 805 vs IFRS 3</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">US GAAP (ASC 805)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IFRS 3)</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Business definition screen test</span><span>Concentration test (ASU 2017-01)</span><span>Similar concentration test (2020 amendment) – converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>NCI measurement</span><span>MANDATORY fair value (full goodwill only)</span><span>CHOICE – full goodwill (fair value) OR partial goodwill (proportionate net assets)</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Bargain purchase gains</span><span>Immediate earnings recognition</span><span>Same – converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Acquisition-related costs</span><span>Expensed as incurred</span><span>Same – converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Measurement period</span><span>Up to one year</span><span>Same – converged</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">The NCI measurement choice is genuinely the ONLY significant divergence left standing in this otherwise thoroughly converged standard – worth remembering as the single comparison point most likely to matter in practice.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 805 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Recognition of identifiable assets/liabilities at fair value</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>At the acquisition date</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Goodwill or bargain purchase gain</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Goodwill capitalised; bargain purchase gain recognised immediately</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Acquisition-related costs</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Expensed as incurred</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Liability-classified contingent consideration remeasurement</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised through earnings each period</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s18"><span class="num">18</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 350</span><span>Governs subsequent goodwill impairment testing following initial recognition here</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 730</span><span>Governs acquired in-process R&D, capitalised at fair value per this Topic's exception to the general expense rule</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 810</span><span>Consolidation – supplies the control determination that triggers this Topic's application in the first place</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s19"><span class="num">19</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Full goodwill method</div><div class="glossary-def">Measuring goodwill as if the entire target were acquired at implied fair value, with NCI measured at fair value – mandatory under US GAAP, optional under IFRS 3.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Partial goodwill method</div><div class="glossary-def">An IFRS 3-only option measuring NCI at its proportionate share of identifiable net assets, excluding NCI's share of goodwill entirely.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.ASC805 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

